# Network Security & Firewall Implementation

## Project Overview

This project focused on designing a secure network and implementing a firewall within a virtual lab environment.

The work included creating a network topology, configuring an OPNsense firewall, reviewing endpoint network settings, and implementing firewall rules to control traffic between systems.

The project reinforced the importance of layered network security, firewall placement, segmentation, access control, and properly configured internal network communication.

## Objectives

- Design a secure network topology.
- Identify the role of key network infrastructure components.
- Configure an OPNsense firewall.
- Review LAN and WAN firewall interfaces.
- Configure and verify endpoint network settings.
- Implement firewall rules for internal traffic control.
- Understand the importance of default-deny behavior.
- Apply layered security concepts to network architecture.

